+    <request name="capture_toplevel_with_size" since="3">
+      <description summary="capture a toplevel within pixel bounds">
+        Same as capture_toplevel_with_wlr_toplevel_handle, with maximum buffer
+        width and height in physical pixels. Zero means unconstrained on that
+        axis; zero on both axes requests the native size.
+
+        The compositor fits the entire native image within these bounds,
+        preserving its aspect ratio to integer-pixel precision, without
+        upscaling. Each dimension is at least one pixel. The buffer events
+        advertise the actual required size; clients must use that size.
